  caveat: The corpus is SYNTHETIC and was written by the same project as the recognizer; several of its classes (cohort 2) were added because the generalisation regression set showed them missing (changes.jsonl C23, C31). It is the best out-of-sample estimate that survives this round, not an independent one.
  caveat: The generalisation regression sets (out/s3/review_generalisation, review_generalisation2) are NO LONGER held out: counter.py, lfsr.py, shift.py, controls.py and verify.py all consulted them (changes.jsonl C25).
  caveat: TEMPO is the development design: every TEMPO figure is in-sample. Four recognizer fixes were traced from TEMPO misses by truth name (changes.jsonl C27-C30), and PC03, PC06, PC07, PC09, C01-C06, C10 and C21(d) were selected on TEMPO.
  caveat: These rates come from ONE seeded corpus evaluation; they carry no confidence interval.
  caveat: They describe the recognizer AND the harness verifier as of source.code_sha256: 'found' means the harness verified the structure, so a change to tools/s3/verify.py moves them as surely as a change to a recognizer module (review[1] issue 2).
  caveat: THE false_positive_structures COLUMN OVERSTATES; found / exact and their denominators do NOT. out/s3/review_generalisation2/evaluate.py's outcomes() builds its item list from truth registers whose kind is in STRUCTURE_KINDS, so a 'flag' register's alt_kinds are never consulted. Under the truth's TOGGLE_RULE a 1-bit toggle is kind 'flag' with alt_kinds ['counter'] -- the truth EXPLICITLY ACCEPTS a counter over it -- yet such a prediction matches no item there and is scored a false positive. Counted on the evaluation this document was derived from, as false-positive structures of width 1 lying entirely in one truth register of kind 'flag': holdout 2 of 6, train 10 of 16. The overstatement is in the CONSERVATIVE direction. tools/s3/score.py -- the scorer every published table comes from -- does not make this error: score.Truth builds accepts from alt_kinds for EVERY truth register, a flag included. The scoring rule is left as it is on purpose: changing it would move a published out-of-sample number without a lead decision (changes.jsonl T04, T14).

